  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (4 witnesses, 2 names, composes nothing), so I used 1 of the 6 runs.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_600_1e.lean`):\n- **Who it applies to:** the subject must belong to the vehicle aggregate, `ru_aggregate(subject, \"DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle\")`.\n- **When it applies:** always (`.tt`). The only condition, \"In any event,\", is already on the node as words that add no condition.\n- **The duty:** `kin_speed(subject) ≤ 80 mph`. The text forbids a speed *greater than* 80 mph, so the duty is \"not greater than\". The 80 mph is written as `Units.mph 80`, in m/s.\n- **Readings I chose:** none. Reading \"drive or operate\" through the vehicle's speed is the node's own narrowing, so I didn't repeat it.\n\n**The witnesses**, each one road user heading east over three instants one second apart, with no structures or devices:\n\n| Scenario | Subject | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | car at 38 m/s (about 85 mph) | violated |\n| permit | car at 33 m/s (about 74 mph) | compliant |\n| idle | pedestrian at 1.4 m/s, not in the vehicle aggregate | not applicable |\n| blind | moving car with no speed recorded, `kin.speed` masked | unknown |\n\nThe node looks correct as written. `task_result.md` is in the working directory.",
